      "writtenOn": "2013-10-09T16:09:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(wishlist) it\u0027d be nice to be able to specify the earliest release where a feature can be removed (both for our own sake and for end users).\n\nthe openstack convention is to be release - 2 backwards compatible on the service side, which implies that a deprecated feature can be removed in release + 2 after being officially deprecated. so i\u0027m envisioning something like:\n\n  @deprecated(as_of\u003dICEHOUSE, in_favor_of\u003d\u0027the v3 API\u0027)\n  def some_api_method(self):\n    pass\n\nresulting in a log such as:\n\n  WARNING: some_api_method is deprecated in favor\n  of v3 API and may be removed in Icehouse + 2 releases.\n\nThis is obviously verbose for deprecating the entire v2 API method by method, so you could have a helper decorator that has the correct arguments pre-set, e.g.:\n\n  @v2_api_deprecated",
      "revId": "4dd9c7a3744c61686be1ea37c2ec550f192987e5",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
